config SHRINK_LRU_TRYLOCK
	bool "Enable asynchronous LRU reclaim daemon"
	default n
	help
	  Reclaim pages that could not be locked by the normal LRU
	  shrinker on the first attempt asynchronously, instead of
	  blocking the caller or dropping the pages back to the LRU.

	  Pages whose trylock fails are collected on a private inactive
	  list (bounded to about 16MB) and a background kthread retries
	  reclaiming them on a CPU that is not the highest-frequency
	  CPU.  This reduces latency spikes caused by contended page
	  locks during direct reclaim.

	  Say Y here to enable the asynchronous LRU reclaim daemon.
	  If unsure, say N.
